{
  "_comment": "Test vectors of proxy-shopping v1 (docs/spec.md), generated by the Go implementation (node/internal/vectors; UPDATE_VECTORS=1 go test ./internal/vectors rewrites this file). keys: public keys per spec §1 for the BIP39 test mnemonic (\"abandon\") and every lab/keys/*.mnemonic; btc_address is the P2WPKH of m/84'/1'/0'/0/0, btc_escrow_xpub the tpub of m/7333'/2'. order: §1.1 idx of order_id, the user-1 and shopper-1 order keys (m/7333'/1'/idx') and the escrow-1 key derived from its tpub (…/idx). btc_escrow: §5.1 witness script (U=user-1, S=shopper-1, E=escrow-1 order keys) and its P2WSH address. safe: §6.2 with the lab EVM accounts of user-1/shopper-1/escrow-1 as owners and placeholder contract addresses; proxy_creation_code is that of the lab SafeProxyFactory (Safe v1.4.1 built with solc 0.8.28; clients must read factory.proxyCreationCode() at run time), canonical_v141 repeats the computation with the code of the canonical mainnet v1.4.1 factory; the CREATE2 addresses use the placeholder factory and singleton. safe_tx: §6.4 EIP-712 hashes for chain_id 31337 and verifying contract = safe.address, with the 65 byte signatures (v=27/28) of the listed owners; joined_signatures are sorted by owner address. delivery: §4.4 ciphertext = base64(nonce || XChaCha20-Poly1305(K, nonce, JSON(address), aad=order id bytes)) where JSON(address) is exactly address_json; key_for_shopper/key_for_escrow are NIP-44 v2 of hex(K) from user-1 with the given nonces; key_for_escrow_sha256 is hex(SHA-256(key_for_escrow payload string)). gift_wrap: §4.1 message from user-1 to shopper-1 with a fixed one-time key and fixed NIP-44 nonces; unwrap wrap with the shopper-1 key to obtain seal and inner. All hex is lower case except EVM addresses (EIP-55). key_proof: §4.4.1 for user-1 and order_id; btc is the BIP340 signature over SHA-256(message) with the user-1 order key and 32 zero bytes of auxiliary randomness (verify with the x-only key of user_btc_pubkey; other aux values give other valid signatures), evm is personal_sign(message) by the user-1 EVM account (RFC 6979, v=27/28). libp2p: §1 libp2p key of the abandon mnemonic (m/7333'/0'/0', secp256k1): secret, 33 byte compressed public key, its libp2p protobuf PublicKey encoding, and the peer id (identity multihash of that encoding, base58btc). p2p: a list bundle of §2.6 as an operator serves it at list_url (in bundle order: the coordinator-1 delegation of operator-1 with the list_url tag, the operator-1 list with p2p_relays, the shopper-1 profile whose p2p.addrs is a /p2p-circuit address through relay-p2p, and the shopper-1 10050), all with created_at = v = 1790000000; reply_p2p of §4.4 for user-1; msg: the lines of /ps/msg/1.0.0 (§10) for the gift_wrap wrap (request_line is exactly JSON(wrap) + \"\\n\" as Go encodes it; receivers must accept any JSON encoding of the event).",
